  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 28/11/2025, the proposal as shown on the drawing(s) submitted on 28/11/2025 and numbered ST01 Rev 02, ST02, Rev 02, ST03 Rev 02, ST04 Rev 02, ST05 Rev 02, ST06 Rev 02, ST07 Rev 02, ST08 Rev 02, ST11 Rev 02, ST12 Rev 02, ST13 Rev 02, ST14 Rev 02, ST15 Rev 02, ST16 Rev 02, ST17 Rev 02, ST18 Rev 02, SR09 Rev 02, consent, photographs was not lawful within the meanings of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 because:\r\n\r\nThe property contains two flats and is not a single dwellinghouse. In Article 2. (1) of the GDPO 2015 (as amended), the definition of a dwellinghouse does not include a building containing one of more flats. Therefore, for the purposes of the GDPO 2015 (as amended), the property does not benefit the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1 Class B of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended) and planning permission would be required\r\n",
    "Reason : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 28/11/2025, the proposal as shown on the drawing(s) submitted on 28/11/2025 and numbered ST01 Rev 02, ST02, Rev 02, ST03 Rev 02, ST04 Rev 02, ST05 Rev 02, ST06 Rev 02, ST07 Rev 02, ST08 Rev 02, ST11 Rev 02, ST12 Rev 02, ST13 Rev 02, ST14 Rev 02, ST15 Rev 02, ST16 Rev 02, ST17 Rev 02, ST18 Rev 02, SR09 Rev 02, consent, photographs was not lawful within the meanings of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 because the property does not benefit from having permitted development rights and therefore planning permission would be required. "
